  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## What's changed\n\nFirst release of the cross-platform façade over the SFMC SDK core bindings.\n\n- **One API on both platforms**: `SfmcSdkClient` with awaitable `InitializeAsync`, `Identity`\n  (profile id / contact key, string attributes) and `TrackCustomEvent`, over\n  [`SFMCSDK.Net.Android 3.1.1.1`](https://github.com/sbokatuk/SFMCSDK.Net.Android/releases/tag/v3.1.1.1)\n  and [`SFMCSDK.Net.iOS 4.0.1.2`](https://github.com/sbokatuk/SFMCSDK.Net.iOS/releases/tag/v4.0.1.2),\n  pinned exactly. The version names the iOS line (SFMCSDK 4.0.1); the Android side is sfmcsdk 3.1.1.\n- **The platform asymmetries are absorbed, not papered over**: Android's `configure` callback\n  becomes an await with an options-driven timeout linked to the caller's `CancellationToken`;\n  iOS completes after the state machine settles, because with zero modules configured its\n  completion block never fires - measured upstream behaviour, encoded in the binding\n  repository's device tests and documented in `Platforms/Apple`.\n- **Sharp edges filed off**: a custom event name the native SDK rejects throws\n  `ArgumentException` on both platforms (raw Android returns null and drops the event; raw iOS\n  returns nil), and a second `InitializeAsync` throws the one-shot guard instead of racing a\n  native configure that upstream forbids repeating.\n- **Nine target frameworks** - `net8.0`, `net9.0`, `net10.0`, each with `-android` and `-ios`\n  heads. The plain assets restore anywhere and throw `PlatformNotSupportedException` naming the\n  platform heads, so shared class libraries, unit tests and a MAUI app's Windows head reference\n  the package with no conditionals.\n- **Nothing is hidden**: the raw namespaces `Com.Salesforce.Marketingcloud.Sfmcsdk` and\n  `SFMCSDK` arrive with the package on their platform - module configuration (MobilePush and\n  friends), consent, the event bus and the rest stay one `using` away.\n- Licence is plain `MIT`: this package ships no native binaries; Salesforce's BSD-3-Clause\n  arrives with the binding packages, each of which declares and packs both texts.",
